The Jammu and Kashmir Heritage Conservation and Preservation Act, 2010
(u)
"object" means any material or physical entity ;
(v)
"owner" includes : -
(i)
a joint owner invested with power of management on his own behalf and other joint owners and successors in title of any
such owner ; and
(ii)
any manager or trustee exercising powers of management and the successor-in-office of any such manager or trustee ;
(w)
"place" means any geographical area or space ;
(x)
"prescribed" means prescribed by rules made under this Act ;
(y)
"preservation" means redeeming or saving any cultural heritage, tangible or intangible, from decay and fading away to
protect and patronize it ;
(z)
"regulations" means regulations made under section 20 of this Act ;
(z-i) "rules" means the rules made under section 19 of this Act ;
(z-ii) "site" means areas, spaces, places, precincts, etc.;
(z-iii) "survey" means preliminary investigation of any tangible or intangible item or object of apparent heritage value with
a view to undertake research and documentation of the same and its subsequent listing for its protection or preservation.
